comments.body:
> [696ddc5](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36496/changes/696ddc5f281c7701bd3e1576b19c9a15f37a6642) _coins: reuse prevout task vector storage_:

The vector is cast to an r-value reference. (The template type becoming an l-value is banned through `!std::is_lvalue_reference_v<R>`).
The argument to `Submit()` is never used to construct a new vector inside the method, which means the storage of the underlying vector is never currently "reaped".
My inference is that the `ThreadPool` was written that way since we move from the individual *elements* of the range.

It would probably be more honest/correct to allow non-const l-values to be passed into `Submit()` and remove the `move()` here. `!std::is_const_v<std::remove_reference_t<R>>` could be sufficient, and the l-value/r-value nature of `R` would be up to the caller as was intended when r-value references were introduced.

<details><summary>Compiling diff</summary>

```diff
diff --git a/src/coins.cpp b/src/coins.cpp
index e32e7f21d8..bf8c2bd766 100644
--- a/src/coins.cpp
+++ b/src/coins.cpp
@@ -397,7 +397,7 @@ CCoinsViewCache::ResetGuard CoinsViewOverlay::StartFetching(const CBlock& block
             m_tasks.assign(std::min(workers_count, m_inputs.size()), [this] {
                 while (ProcessInput()) {}
             });
-            if (auto futures{m_thread_pool->Submit(std::move(m_tasks))}) {
+            if (auto futures{m_thread_pool->Submit(m_tasks)}) {
                 m_futures = std::move(*futures);
             } else {
                 // Submit can fail if a shared owner of the thread pool outside of this class calls Stop() or
diff --git a/src/util/threadpool.h b/src/util/threadpool.h
index 6c16851525..421f956367 100644
--- a/src/util/threadpool.h
+++ b/src/util/threadpool.h
@@ -216,7 +216,7 @@ public:
      *          uncaught exceptions, as they would otherwise be silently discarded.
      */
     template <std::ranges::sized_range R>
-        requires(!std::is_lvalue_reference_v<R>)
+        requires(!std::is_const_v<std::remove_reference_t<R>>)
     [[nodiscard]] util::Expected<std::vector<RangeFuture<R>>, SubmitError> Submit(R&& fns) noexcept EXCLUSIVE_LOCKS_REQUIRED(!m_mutex)
     {
         std::vector<RangeFuture<R>> futures;
